1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,690
If your knee replacement
still hurts

2
00:00:02,690 --> 00:00:05,170
and the X-ray keeps coming
back fine,

3
00:00:05,170 --> 00:00:06,360
don't accept that.

4
00:00:06,400 --> 00:00:07,700
I've been putting down
hardwood

5
00:00:07,700 --> 00:00:09,410
floors for thirty years.

6
00:00:09,850 --> 00:00:11,670
Kneeling on the boards all
day,

7
00:00:11,670 --> 00:00:13,720
nailing them down one by
one.

8
00:00:14,070 --> 00:00:14,910
I had my right knee

9
00:00:14,910 --> 00:00:16,480
replaced two years ago.

10
00:00:16,570 --> 00:00:18,640
It has hurt every day
since.

11
00:00:19,010 --> 00:00:20,920
Not surgery pain.

12
00:00:21,090 --> 00:00:22,370
I know what that felt
like,

13
00:00:22,370 --> 00:00:23,510
and it went away.

14
00:00:23,750 --> 00:00:24,770
This is different.

15
00:00:24,810 --> 00:00:25,500
Tight.

16
00:00:25,550 --> 00:00:26,220
Full.

17
00:00:26,260 --> 00:00:27,170
Like a band around

18
00:00:27,170 --> 00:00:28,850
the joint that never
loosens.

19
00:00:29,090 --> 00:00:30,200
And for two years I've

20
00:00:30,200 --> 00:00:31,540
been told the same thing.

21
00:00:31,870 --> 00:00:32,780
Give it time.

22
00:00:32,960 --> 00:00:34,980
At six weeks it was
swelling,

23
00:00:34,980 --> 00:00:36,290
and swelling is normal.

24
00:00:36,420 --> 00:00:37,340
At three months,

25
00:00:37,340 --> 00:00:38,310
give it six.

26
00:00:38,350 --> 00:00:39,310
At six months,

27
00:00:39,310 --> 00:00:41,050
some knees take a full
year.

28
00:00:41,090 --> 00:00:42,150
At a year,

29
00:00:42,150 --> 00:00:44,280
eighteen months isn't
unusual.

30
00:00:44,420 --> 00:00:45,700
And I didn't just wait.

31
00:00:45,760 --> 00:00:47,110
We went down the list.

32
00:00:47,290 --> 00:00:48,710
More physical therapy.

33
00:00:48,950 --> 00:00:49,950
Every session,

34
00:00:49,950 --> 00:00:51,520
every exercise at home.

35
00:00:51,740 --> 00:00:52,910
I got stronger.

36
00:00:52,990 --> 00:00:54,520
The tightness never moved.

37
00:00:54,610 --> 00:00:56,030
The pain pills helped,

38
00:00:56,030 --> 00:00:57,280
and that was the problem.

39
00:00:57,420 --> 00:00:59,380
I'm already on enough
every morning,

40
00:00:59,380 --> 00:01:00,470
and nobody could tell me

41
00:01:00,470 --> 00:01:01,660
when I'd get to stop.

42
00:01:02,060 --> 00:01:03,270
Then a nerve block.

43
00:01:03,310 --> 00:01:04,970
Then talk of burning the
nerve.

44
00:01:05,110 --> 00:01:06,300
And after that, a second

45
00:01:06,300 --> 00:01:07,400
operation to go back

46
00:01:07,400 --> 00:01:08,590
in and do it over.

47
00:01:08,690 --> 00:01:09,720
I said no.

48
00:01:09,950 --> 00:01:11,550
Every morning I stepped
out of bed

49
00:01:11,550 --> 00:01:12,560
and my knee felt like

50
00:01:12,560 --> 00:01:14,310
a band was wrapped around
it,

51
00:01:14,310 --> 00:01:16,750
tightening every inch I
tried to straighten.

52
00:01:17,050 --> 00:01:18,260
Every morning I took
something

53
00:01:18,260 --> 00:01:19,830
for it and went to work.

54
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:21,480
Couldn't do the stairs,

55
00:01:21,480 --> 00:01:22,520
couldn't stand at the
counter

56
00:01:22,520 --> 00:01:24,150
long enough to finish
dinner,

57
00:01:24,150 --> 00:01:25,600
couldn't sit through my
granddaughter's

58
00:01:25,600 --> 00:01:27,840
game without shifting
every two minutes.

59
00:01:28,030 --> 00:01:28,820
At work,

60
00:01:28,820 --> 00:01:30,250
the young guys on my crew
started

61
00:01:30,250 --> 00:01:31,620
laying my boards for me.

62
00:01:31,850 --> 00:01:33,100
Nobody said anything.

63
00:01:33,490 --> 00:01:35,090
It woke me at night,

64
00:01:35,090 --> 00:01:37,050
and it turned ordinary
things,

65
00:01:37,050 --> 00:01:38,280
like getting in the truck

66
00:01:38,280 --> 00:01:39,300
or up off the floor,

67
00:01:39,300 --> 00:01:40,370
into a decision.

68
00:01:40,680 --> 00:01:42,120
After a long and serious

69
00:01:42,120 --> 00:01:43,010
talk with my wife,

70
00:01:43,010 --> 00:01:44,810
I went back in one more
time.

71
00:01:45,170 --> 00:01:46,360
That was the fourth set

72
00:01:46,360 --> 00:01:47,910
of X-rays on this knee.

73
00:01:48,230 --> 00:01:49,730
And like the three before
it,

74
00:01:49,730 --> 00:01:52,490
the answer was everything
looks great.

75
00:01:52,530 --> 00:01:54,970
No loosening, no
infection,

76
00:01:54,970 --> 00:01:55,970
nothing wrong.

77
00:01:56,290 --> 00:01:57,720
Only this time

78
00:01:57,720 --> 00:01:59,120
there was no new number.

79
00:01:59,160 --> 00:02:01,800
Nobody said give it
another six months.

80
00:02:01,850 --> 00:02:03,600
There was nothing left to
give it.

81
00:02:03,810 --> 00:02:04,830
I sat in the parking

82
00:02:04,830 --> 00:02:05,830
lot for a while.

83
00:02:05,940 --> 00:02:06,990
Okay, I thought.

84
00:02:07,160 --> 00:02:08,640
Then explain this.

85
00:02:08,980 --> 00:02:11,070
Anyway, a couple of months
back,

86
00:02:11,070 --> 00:02:12,530
I hit my breaking point.

87
00:02:12,860 --> 00:02:14,900
It was around 2:30 in the
morning.

88
00:02:15,100 --> 00:02:17,050
Everyone in the house was
asleep

89
00:02:17,050 --> 00:02:18,790
and I was downstairs in
the recliner

90
00:02:18,790 --> 00:02:19,910
with my leg up,

91
00:02:19,910 --> 00:02:21,550
trying to find any angle
where

92
00:02:21,550 --> 00:02:23,150
it didn't feel like
something was wrapped

93
00:02:23,150 --> 00:02:25,200
around my knee and
tightening.

94
00:02:25,520 --> 00:02:27,830
My wife didn't know I'd
come downstairs.

95
00:02:27,910 --> 00:02:29,580
By then I'd stopped
telling her.

96
00:02:29,790 --> 00:02:30,380
I had a floor

97
00:02:30,380 --> 00:02:31,470
to start at seven.

98
00:02:31,620 --> 00:02:32,700
And I just thought,

99
00:02:32,700 --> 00:02:34,120
is this really my life
now?

100
00:02:34,160 --> 00:02:35,540
I can't live like this.

101
00:02:35,730 --> 00:02:37,300
Thirty years of floors,

102
00:02:37,300 --> 00:02:38,260
and I couldn't see how

103
00:02:38,260 --> 00:02:39,530
I'd get through one more.

104
00:02:39,690 --> 00:02:41,360
So I made myself a
promise.

105
00:02:41,620 --> 00:02:42,530
I wouldn't go a day

106
00:02:42,530 --> 00:02:44,030
without looking for an
answer.

107
00:02:44,280 --> 00:02:45,710
And when I found one,

108
00:02:45,710 --> 00:02:46,850
I'd share it with everyone

109
00:02:46,850 --> 00:02:48,310
going through the same
thing.

110
00:02:48,470 --> 00:02:49,420
So I got my laptop

111
00:02:49,420 --> 00:02:50,480
out and went looking.

112
00:02:50,800 --> 00:02:52,080
Not for a product.

113
00:02:52,220 --> 00:02:53,510
For an explanation.

114
00:02:53,810 --> 00:02:55,480
Mayo Clinic forums,

115
00:02:55,480 --> 00:02:57,650
the knee replacement group
on Facebook,

116
00:02:57,650 --> 00:03:00,250
doctor videos, medical
animations.

117
00:03:00,590 --> 00:03:02,030
And that's when I found a
video

118
00:03:02,030 --> 00:03:03,860
from a physical therapist
named Dr.

119
00:03:03,900 --> 00:03:05,140
Steven Salinger,

120
00:03:05,140 --> 00:03:06,290
whose own wife

121
00:03:06,290 --> 00:03:08,160
had been through exactly
this.

122
00:03:08,300 --> 00:03:10,450
But before I say anything
else,

123
00:03:10,450 --> 00:03:11,890
I want to be straight with
you.

124
00:03:12,280 --> 00:03:14,860
You've already had
something work fast.

125
00:03:14,940 --> 00:03:15,800
The ice.

126
00:03:15,890 --> 00:03:17,470
The first week of a new
pill.

127
00:03:17,510 --> 00:03:19,330
The good day after a
session.

128
00:03:19,680 --> 00:03:20,620
Then it wore off.

129
00:03:20,660 --> 00:03:23,200
That's the part nobody
warns you about.

130
00:03:23,400 --> 00:03:25,310
Fast relief isn't relief.

131
00:03:25,500 --> 00:03:26,620
It's a preview.

132
00:03:26,840 --> 00:03:27,740
So I'm not going to tell

133
00:03:27,740 --> 00:03:28,810
you this works fast.

134
00:03:28,850 --> 00:03:29,710
It doesn't.

135
00:03:29,820 --> 00:03:31,720
But if you're willing to
be patient,

136
00:03:31,720 --> 00:03:32,540
and to look at what's

137
00:03:32,540 --> 00:03:34,050
going on around your new
knee

138
00:03:34,050 --> 00:03:35,640
instead of inside it,
there

139
00:03:35,640 --> 00:03:37,920
is a real reason it still
hurts.

140
00:03:38,120 --> 00:03:39,890
And something you can do
about it.

141
00:03:40,060 --> 00:03:41,880
Let me explain what he
said,

142
00:03:41,880 --> 00:03:43,340
because this is what
changed

143
00:03:43,340 --> 00:03:44,510
everything for me.

144
00:03:44,650 --> 00:03:46,260
He started with the
basics.

145
00:03:46,480 --> 00:03:47,860
A knee replacement takes
out

146
00:03:47,860 --> 00:03:49,590
the worn joint surfaces
and puts

147
00:03:49,590 --> 00:03:50,870
in metal and plastic.

148
00:03:51,080 --> 00:03:53,020
That's what stops the
arthritis pain

149
00:03:53,020 --> 00:03:54,650
you had before the
operation.

150
00:03:55,020 --> 00:03:56,490
That part I already knew.

151
00:03:56,660 --> 00:03:57,990
But then he explained
something

152
00:03:57,990 --> 00:03:59,510
nobody had ever told me.

153
00:03:59,640 --> 00:04:00,400
He said,

154
00:04:00,400 --> 00:04:01,730
think about a swollen foot

155
00:04:01,730 --> 00:04:02,830
inside a shoe.

156
00:04:03,140 --> 00:04:04,650
The shoe didn't shrink.

157
00:04:04,750 --> 00:04:06,880
Your foot is taking up
more room,

158
00:04:06,880 --> 00:04:08,570
so everything feels
cramped

159
00:04:08,570 --> 00:04:10,150
and tight and squeezed.

160
00:04:10,540 --> 00:04:12,210
Your new knee sits in a
limited

161
00:04:12,210 --> 00:04:14,110
space with living tissue

162
00:04:14,110 --> 00:04:15,680
packed all around it.

163
00:04:15,960 --> 00:04:17,740
To put that knee in, the
surgeon

164
00:04:17,740 --> 00:04:19,360
had to work through that
tissue.

165
00:04:19,650 --> 00:04:21,870
Afterwards it gets
inflamed and swollen.

166
00:04:21,950 --> 00:04:23,830
At first that's normal.

167
00:04:24,090 --> 00:04:25,610
But in some people that
swelling can

168
00:04:25,610 --> 00:04:28,200
stay switched on far
longer than expected.

169
00:04:28,280 --> 00:04:29,850
And swollen tissue takes
up more

170
00:04:29,850 --> 00:04:31,600
room than calm tissue
does.

171
00:04:31,850 --> 00:04:33,760
So when you bend,

172
00:04:33,760 --> 00:04:35,600
that tissue gets
compressed.

173
00:04:35,900 --> 00:04:37,090
When you straighten,

174
00:04:37,090 --> 00:04:38,450
it gets pulled tight.

175
00:04:38,600 --> 00:04:39,440
That's the band.

176
00:04:39,480 --> 00:04:40,550
That's the ache

177
00:04:40,550 --> 00:04:42,170
that never quite leaves.

178
00:04:42,210 --> 00:04:43,310
And you start being

179
00:04:43,310 --> 00:04:44,620
the one who says,

180
00:04:44,620 --> 00:04:45,630
you go ahead.

181
00:04:45,670 --> 00:04:46,780
I'll stay here.

182
00:04:47,010 --> 00:04:48,540
And that's exactly why

183
00:04:48,540 --> 00:04:50,200
so much of what I'd tried

184
00:04:50,200 --> 00:04:51,190
hadn't worked.

185
00:04:51,230 --> 00:04:53,180
Physical therapy
strengthens the muscles

186
00:04:53,180 --> 00:04:54,090
around the knee.

187
00:04:54,250 --> 00:04:55,270
Worth doing,

188
00:04:55,270 --> 00:04:56,100
and I'd done it.

189
00:04:56,330 --> 00:04:57,720
It does nothing about
tissue

190
00:04:57,720 --> 00:04:58,840
taking up room.

191
00:04:59,080 --> 00:05:00,450
A nerve block quiets

192
00:05:00,450 --> 00:05:02,020
the nerve carrying the
signal.

193
00:05:02,280 --> 00:05:03,850
It doesn't touch

194
00:05:03,850 --> 00:05:05,110
what's generating it.

195
00:05:05,340 --> 00:05:06,810
But when that irritated
tissue

196
00:05:06,810 --> 00:05:08,430
finally calms down,

197
00:05:08,430 --> 00:05:09,840
it holds less fluid,

198
00:05:09,840 --> 00:05:11,320
and it takes up less room.

199
00:05:11,550 --> 00:05:14,440
Less room taken up means
less pressure

200
00:05:14,440 --> 00:05:15,820
squeezing the joint.

201
00:05:15,860 --> 00:05:17,400
That's what takes the
pressure off.

202
00:05:17,820 --> 00:05:19,310
After two years of this,

203
00:05:19,310 --> 00:05:20,910
it finally made sense.

204
00:05:21,220 --> 00:05:23,150
The problem was never the
new knee.

205
00:05:23,280 --> 00:05:25,190
It was the tissue crowded
around it.

206
00:05:25,540 --> 00:05:27,050
He calls it the squeeze.

207
00:05:27,140 --> 00:05:29,580
Once you've felt it,
that's the word.

208
00:05:29,850 --> 00:05:31,750
I'd bought knee sleeves,

209
00:05:31,750 --> 00:05:34,570
gel knee pads, compression
braces,

210
00:05:34,570 --> 00:05:36,860
creams, half of Amazon
really,

211
00:05:36,860 --> 00:05:37,890
and all any of it gave

212
00:05:37,890 --> 00:05:38,950
me was an hour.

213
00:05:39,470 --> 00:05:40,370
I even looked at going

214
00:05:40,370 --> 00:05:42,290
to a clinic for the light
therapy.

215
00:05:42,420 --> 00:05:44,450
But at $200 a session

216
00:05:44,450 --> 00:05:45,980
with nothing covered by
insurance,

217
00:05:45,980 --> 00:05:47,490
that was a quick no.

218
00:05:47,560 --> 00:05:48,870
Then one night I went

219
00:05:48,870 --> 00:05:50,140
back to that knee
replacement

220
00:05:50,140 --> 00:05:51,810
group and actually read
it.

221
00:05:52,090 --> 00:05:53,470
Thousands of people,

222
00:05:53,470 --> 00:05:55,310
years out from surgery,

223
00:05:55,310 --> 00:05:56,780
comparing notes on
stiffness

224
00:05:56,780 --> 00:05:58,820
and tightness nobody could
explain.

225
00:05:59,100 --> 00:06:00,820
And no matter how far I
scrolled,

226
00:06:00,820 --> 00:06:02,790
the same thing kept coming
up.

227
00:06:03,020 --> 00:06:04,650
This one device,

228
00:06:04,650 --> 00:06:06,560
and people saying it was
the first

229
00:06:06,560 --> 00:06:07,980
thing that made a
difference.

230
00:06:08,260 --> 00:06:10,090
And before anyone jumps in
thinking,

231
00:06:10,090 --> 00:06:11,870
alright, here it comes,

232
00:06:11,870 --> 00:06:13,380
he's selling me something,

233
00:06:13,380 --> 00:06:15,240
let me shut that down
right now.

234
00:06:15,510 --> 00:06:17,380
I'm only here because I
made myself

235
00:06:17,380 --> 00:06:19,770
a promise at 2:30 in the
morning

236
00:06:19,770 --> 00:06:20,760
that if I ever found

237
00:06:20,760 --> 00:06:22,030
something that helped,

238
00:06:22,030 --> 00:06:23,090
I'd say so.

239
00:06:23,440 --> 00:06:25,280
It's called the KenRelief
Red

240
00:06:25,280 --> 00:06:26,710
Light Therapy Wrap.

241
00:06:27,210 --> 00:06:29,220
At first glance I didn't
buy it.

242
00:06:29,470 --> 00:06:31,090
It looked like the cheap
knee sleeves

243
00:06:31,090 --> 00:06:33,180
off Amazon that did
nothing for me.

244
00:06:33,330 --> 00:06:35,330
But I went to their
website anyway,

245
00:06:35,330 --> 00:06:36,170
just to see what all

246
00:06:36,170 --> 00:06:37,250
the fuss was about.

247
00:06:37,570 --> 00:06:39,430
It's the same red light
therapy clinics

248
00:06:39,430 --> 00:06:41,770
charge $200 a session for,

249
00:06:41,770 --> 00:06:44,510
off machines that cost
fifty thousand dollars,

250
00:06:44,510 --> 00:06:45,440
in a wrap you plug

251
00:06:45,440 --> 00:06:46,590
into the wall at home.

252
00:06:46,660 --> 00:06:48,310
Two hundred and forty
lights.

253
00:06:48,560 --> 00:06:50,490
Red at 660 nanometers

254
00:06:50,490 --> 00:06:52,610
and near-infrared at 850,

255
00:06:52,610 --> 00:06:54,810
run together for the
strongest effect.

256
00:06:54,990 --> 00:06:56,740
Four strength levels.

257
00:06:57,130 --> 00:06:58,950
A five to thirty minute
timer.

258
00:06:58,990 --> 00:07:00,480
Then I saw the guarantee.

259
00:07:00,520 --> 00:07:01,670
Ninety days.

260
00:07:01,740 --> 00:07:04,470
Results or your money
back,

261
00:07:04,470 --> 00:07:07,090
no questions, no store
credit,

262
00:07:07,090 --> 00:07:08,720
and you don't even send it
back.

263
00:07:08,920 --> 00:07:11,300
No physical therapist ever
gave me ninety

264
00:07:11,300 --> 00:07:12,840
days to change my mind.

265
00:07:12,900 --> 00:07:14,510
There wasn't much to lose,

266
00:07:14,510 --> 00:07:15,680
so I ordered it.

267
00:07:15,770 --> 00:07:17,080
Two of them, actually.

268
00:07:17,280 --> 00:07:19,260
Only the right knee was
replaced,

269
00:07:19,260 --> 00:07:21,260
but you favor the leg that
hurts,

270
00:07:21,260 --> 00:07:22,980
and I'd done it for two
years.

271
00:07:23,260 --> 00:07:25,250
The left one was carrying
the difference.

272
00:07:25,290 --> 00:07:26,200
When it came,

273
00:07:26,200 --> 00:07:28,280
I strapped it on expecting
nothing,

274
00:07:28,280 --> 00:07:29,330
because I'd been let down

275
00:07:29,330 --> 00:07:31,140
too many times to get
excited.

276
00:07:31,420 --> 00:07:32,910
What I felt was warmth.

277
00:07:32,950 --> 00:07:34,810
Not a heating pad kind of
hot.

278
00:07:34,890 --> 00:07:36,420
More like it was coming
from inside

279
00:07:36,420 --> 00:07:37,980
the knee and spreading
around it.

280
00:07:38,220 --> 00:07:39,270
And that was it.

281
00:07:39,320 --> 00:07:40,830
That was the whole
experience.

282
